Subject: [PATCH 02461/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE C
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING; mandated; BUILD ON the .402 win) -- DEPLOY the
 learned action-cost heuristic into the standing planner + PROVE it COMPOUNDS,
 with an LLM-generated-heuristic stronger-arm probe. .402 (exp4353) PROVED the
 mechanism: a learned A* action-cost heuristic trained on solved-level traces
 cut HELD-OUT env-actions-to-solve 25->16 (positive control passed,
 reproduction-gated, verifier_is_oracle=false). The PRD's
 continuous-self-learning vision is learning that COMPOUNDS at inference speed
 ('Carnot must get smarter over time; every solve makes the next faster').
 .403 advances it two ways: (1) DEPLOY -- wire the learned action-cost
 heuristic into arc_solver_kit as the standing A* cost so EVERY future ARC
 solve is action-minimal by default; (2) PROVE IT COMPOUNDS -- measure
 held-out env-actions-to-solve as a FUNCTION of the number of solved-level
 traces in the training corpus (a learning curve: does more experience ->
 fewer actions on held-out levels?), with the positive control distinguishing
 'compounds' from 'no-headroom'. Optional stronger-arm probe: an LLM-generated
 heuristic PROGRAM per game (arXiv:2503.18809 classical planning with
 LLM-generated heuristics) selected by reproduced held-out action count, vs
 the linear heuristic -- on FRESH held-out levels with static-analysis
 receipts + reproduction gates. Emit action_efficiency_compounds BARE bool :=
 (held-out actions-to-solve DECREASES as the solved-trace corpus grows,
 positive control confirming headroom). verifier_is_oracle=false. Cross-game
 VALUE-TRANSFER is RETIRED (exp4342); this is the WORKING per-game mechanism
 DEPLOYED + measured for compounding. NO TRM training.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
